From b8b534591cba8ca7cd43943a655ee6e2591cf5de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:15:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] C backend: runtime option sites (--option-sites)

A game's optional behaviours (Better Wind Waker's settings in BlueWake) are
listed as option sites: an instruction and its replacement, or a place where
the runtime's native code runs. The C backend emits both behaviours at each
site behind dolrecomp_option_flags[option], which the runtime owns, so every
combination of options runs from one translation.

  WHERE OPTION insn|imm16|hook|after VALUE   (WHERE: a DOL address or
                                              module.rel+OFFSET)

A site is a block of its own, a local branch a site substitutes lands on a
block start, and a loop with a site stays in the flat function. A hook calls
dolrecomp_native_hook(ctx, id), which returns 0 to go on or the guest address
to continue at. Chunks with sites declare the two symbols themselves, so
generated.h is unchanged, and without --option-sites the output is
byte-identical (GZLE01's main.dol checked). tests/test_option_sites.c covers
parsing, REL resolution, the CFG and the emitted code.
